# ADR-004: Develop locally first and gate AWS provisioning on cost controls

- Status: Accepted
- Date: 2026-08-23

## Context

Managed Kubernetes and associated cloud networking can create avoidable costs while application and delivery patterns are still changing. A personal portfolio project must make its operating cost visible and controllable.

## Decision

The first functional vertical slice will run locally using Kind or k3d. AWS deployment begins only after a documented monthly budget ceiling, budget alerts, resource-tagging convention, and teardown procedure exist.

Terraform remains the only supported way to create or change cloud resources.

## Consequences

- Early development is cheaper and faster.
- Local and cloud differences must be documented rather than ignored.
- Cloud resources may not be created manually for convenience.
- Cost-management evidence becomes part of the portfolio case study.
